# The Test Cabinet — gallery site environment file (`@clockwyrks/site`).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.site` beside it (apps/site/) and fill in a real value:
#
#     cp apps/site/.env.site.example apps/site/.env.site
#
# The Vite build loads `.env.site` from the site project root before reading
# TCAB_SNAPSHOT_URL. Variables already exported in your shell take precedence
# over the file. The deploy pipeline sets the variable itself (see
# scripts/ci/deploy-site.sh) instead of using a file.
#
# `.env.site` is gitignored; this `.env.site.example` is committed with a
# placeholder value only.

# The public base of the snapshot bucket, which the build writes into the page
# and the page reads the published dataset from in the browser. Unset, the
# gallery reads nothing and renders its empty states. The bucket answers the
# page across origins, so its CORS policy must admit the development server's
# origin for a development server to read it.
TCAB_SNAPSHOT_URL=https://snapshot.example.com
